# Semgrep skip-list.
#
# Every entry here is a known-violation burn-down target. The CI gate
# ships with these excluded so the rule set lands without a big-bang
# cleanup PR; operators then migrate one file at a time and remove
# the entry. Stale entries (the underlying code has changed) get
# caught by the quarterly security review.
#
# Format mirrors .gitignore. Add a comment above each entry with the
# rule id and a ticket or branch reference.

# ---- Defaults (standard) --------------------------------------------------
node_modules
.git
vendor
web/dist
clients
proto/gen
*.min.js
*.pb.go
*.pb.gw.go

# ---- Burn-down entries ----------------------------------------------------
#
# Rule: vaultdms-direct-xff-read / vaultdms-direct-xrealip-read
# Fix: migrate to pkg/trustedproxy. ADR 0031 / T-D-2.
# Already fixed on `wave-15` branch (merges with PR #30). The entries
# here are a stopgap until that branch lands on main.
pkg/gateway/ratelimit.go
pkg/middleware/requestlog.go

# Rule: vaultdms-direct-xff-read
# Owner-service handlers that still read XFF for audit/log context.
# Migrating these to trustedproxy.RealClientIPString() is a follow-up
# ticket per service owner. No security regression (the middleware
# chain normalises XFF upstream), but the invariant should hold.
services/auth/internal/handler/handler.go
services/auth/internal/handler/saml_handler.go
services/signature/internal/handler/handler.go

# Rule: vaultdms-no-http-defaultclient
# Fixed on the techdebt-t3-t9 branch (PR #33). The dsr_crossservice
# file was included there but the scope was originally T-D-5
